I fixed 5 of the 13 bugs (positions 21 to 33) and opened a draft PR for each. The other 8 need your word or a design decision first. All five fixes are built and unit-tested only. Nobody has opened them in AutoCAD.

**Fixed, each in its own draft PR against Civil 3.0.73:**
1. **BUG-1142, PR #1752 (data loss):** one damaged pit record no longer stops every new pipe linking to its pits. CE now names the damaged pit on the command line and leaves it alone.
2. **BUG-1189, PR #1756 (wrong level):** once the survey Xref has been moved since you approved it, New Pit stops offering levels from the old position and says why. The CDSURVEY status then reads "NEEDS A REREAD".
3. **BUG-1190, PR #1755 (wrong level):** a level inside a block in a rotated survey Xref is now stored where the drawing shows it, at 0,10 instead of 10,0.
4. **BUG-1194, PR #1757:** CDTEXTSEG moves the label to the pipe leg you clicked, not the leg round the corner.
5. **BUG-1106, PR #1761:** a rating report naming Glen Eira (or any two-word council) now sets a council CE can actually find.

**Tests:** each fix has new tests, and they fail on the current build before the fix. The full Civil suite ran about 19,800 tests per branch:
- #1752, #1756 and #1757 had 0 failures.
- #1755 had 2 failures. One window test timed out under load and passed when re-run. The other is a PDF test that also passed later, twice on this branch and twice on the current build without my changes.
- #1761 had 1 failure, the same PDF test. I didn't re-run it on that branch.

Three new Settings switches are ON by default because they guard bug fixes. None has a Settings page row yet.

**Skipped, options and my recommendation for each are in the report:**
- **Need your engineering word:** BUG-1088 (the pipe sizer allows grades as steep as 1 in 1), BUG-1095 (council minimum C, open questions C16/C19), BUG-1099 (Maroondah time of concentration, open question C17) and BUG-1091 (DN450 and larger minimum grade).
- **Need a design or window decision:** BUG-1192 (how a long-section stretch with no usable survey is drawn) and BUG-1031 (the missing "Delete cell" menu item).
- **BUG-865:** the slow double-click needs timing in a survey drawing first.
- **BUG-816:** not shown to be a fault. The message comes from the label tidy that always runs after MOVE, not the Tidy labels setting.

**Build lock:** the two sister batches held the shared build lock almost continuously, and 50 minutes of waiting got me no turn. After that, 27 of my 38 build and test steps ran without the lock at low priority, each in its own working copy.

**Still to check in AutoCAD:** each PR has numbered "Real-AutoCAD check" steps.

The report is pushed to `C:\CE_PLAN\areas\release-v3-colleagues-PILOT_CRITICAL_BATCH3_REPORT.md`.

**Summary:** Positions 21 to 33: five fixed in draft PRs #1752, #1755, #1756, #1757 and #1761 (BUG-1142, BUG-1190, BUG-1189, BUG-1194, BUG-1106). All are unit-tested with full Civil suites of about 19,800 tests, and none has been opened in AutoCAD. Eight skipped with options: BUG-1088, BUG-1095, BUG-1099 and BUG-1091 need your word, BUG-1192 and BUG-1031 need design decisions, BUG-865 needs timing, and BUG-816 needs a Settings decision.
